.Dd November 23, 2026
.Dt HMKTVM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hmktvm
.Nd run the hmarket searches used for a virtual-machine host
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm hmktvm
.Op Ar hmarket-flags ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a
.Xr sh 1
wrapper.
Run it from the repository directory.
It calls
.Pa ./hmarket
three times and prints a label before each table.
Extra arguments are appended to every call.
.Pp
The three searches, in order:
.Bl -tag -width "2disk 8gb storage <=$72 >=128G ram" -compact
.It 2disk 8gb storage <=$50 >=64G ram
.Fl c Cm 2
.Fl s Cm 8000
.Fl p Cm 50
.Fl m Cm 64
.It 2disk 4gb storage <=$40 >=64G ram
.Fl c Cm 2
.Fl s Cm 4000
.Fl p Cm 40
.Fl m Cm 64
.It 2disk 8gb storage <=$72 >=128G ram
.Fl c Cm 2
.Fl s Cm 8000
.Fl p Cm 72
.Fl m Cm 128
.El
.Pp
The labels say dollars.
The
.Fl p
value is the auction price in euros.
.Fl s
is gigabytes, with a snapshot
.Ql TB
multiplied by 1000, so 8000 is 8 TB in that unit.
ECC and Enterprise HDD stay on.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exit status is the status of the last
.Xr hmarket 1
call.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hmarket 1 ,
.Xr hmktst 1 ,
.Xr hmktvm-picky 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Todd T. Fries Aq Mt todd@fries.net
